# Internship search

Read `job-finder/internship-preferences.md` before searching. Save a role only when it matches that file. Skip full-time jobs, new-grad roles, and anything the preferences file says to skip. Do not treat "Still open" as a filter.

Look on Handshake, LinkedIn, and company career pages. Follow the finding schedule in the preferences file. Stop after about 10 new listings, then check back.

Write each posting once in `job-finder/jobs.md` and once in `job-finder/application-tracker.csv`. If the application link is already in either file, update that listing instead of adding another.

- A clear match goes under `## Matches`.
- A close match goes under `## Review`, with **Why review:** naming the gap. A posting that never states pay is skipped, not reviewed.
- Set **Application status:** to `Not applied` unless Nevaeh has already applied.
- Keep both files in date-posted order, earliest first, inside each jobs section and in the tracker.

```markdown
## 2026-08-04 — Data Science Intern, Example Co

- **Role:** Data Science Intern
- **Company:** Example Co
- **Date posted:** 2026-08-04
- **Requirements:** B.S. in progress, Python, statistics
- **Internship timeline:** May 2027 – August 2027
- **Deadline:** 2026-10-15
- **Application link:** https://example.com/apply
- **Application status:** Not applied
```

```csv
2026-08-04,Data Science Intern,Example Co,May 2027 – August 2027,2026-10-15,https://example.com/apply,Not applied,,
```

Do not invent a date, a deadline, a link, or pay. Write `Not listed` when the posting omits a date or deadline. Put listings with no post date after every dated listing.

Nevaeh tailors a resume for each application. Do not choose a stock resume for her.

Leave the preferences file unchanged unless Nevaeh edits it.
